sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-26> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "It is likely that in most meaningful senses there is no general way to determine whether any path of a multiway or non-deterministic system yields a given outcome in a number of steps growing only polynomially, i.e. P is not equal to NP.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "P is likely different from NP";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 12, “The Principle of Computational Equivalence”; section “Undecidability and Intractability” (from p. 753), p. 766. Scope: computational complexity of problems about multiway systems and non-deterministic Turing machines"
}
